# The vLLM pin: the latest GitHub release, the image repository of each flavor, the row each
# flavor serves by default, which moves with the release rather than on demand, and native vLLM's
# Python. One release serves every flavor: host/vllm.sh names the image <repository>:<release>,
# in the repository of the flavor it resolves (vllm_flavor). cuda's is the release's default tag,
# vLLM's CUDA 13.0 multi-arch build, not a variant such as -efa: every pinned release since v0.31.0
# publishes it for arm64, v0.34.0 among them (its arm64 image,
# sha256:e40eb98263fa13418dda684147d73e8ec4a2b0e056a37e955dc189cd1b11dd16 on Docker Hub on
# 2026-11-17). rocm's is vLLM's official ROCm image of the same release, its default tag. Sourced
# by scripts/currency.sh, which reads only the release, and host/vllm.sh, and through it
# host/vllm-native.sh.
#
# On v0.34.0, rocm's default tag is its only ROCm build, ROCm 10.0, the same image as
# v0.34.0-rocm100 (index sha256:3cb773d23f063afa86291ef75773cdd486154ddea94c213300f4ed7cc42b7af1
# on Docker Hub on 2026-11-17), the most recent ROCm AMD supports on the Framework's gfx1151.
# v0.34.0 publishes no ROCm 7.2 build ("ROCm 7.2 artifacts dropped", vLLM #61939), so the pin
# names no fallback build: the architect removed the ROCm 7.2 fallback v0.33.0 kept
# (spike-model-gateway's docs/findings/priority.md), since the Framework's rows served on ROCm
# 10.0 throughout. The audio image builds on the same image (host/vllm-rocm-audio/Dockerfile),
# which records its digest where the build pins it.
#
# A row is a model and its server flags, in the rows file VLLM_ROWS names, beside this one.
# VLLM_MODEL_CUDA and VLLM_MODEL_ROCM name each flavor's default row; a VLLM_MODEL in the
# environment names another for one run, with no edit here (docs/engines/vllm/models.md,
# "Changing the model").
#
# v0.34.0 changes how every row's KV cache is laid out and sized, with no flag of the rows' moved
# (its release notes, "Before you upgrade"):
# - The extensible KV cache is on by default on CUDA and ROCm (#56492): the cache is sized from
#   the memory actually free after CUDA graph capture and warmup, not from an estimate. Each row's
#   --gpu-memory-utilization still caps its instance, so the rows that share a host keep their
#   shares, and the cache may grow within the fraction; vLLM notes per-token decode latency can
#   rise on some models. A row that sizes its cache in bytes (--kv-cache-memory-bytes, the agent's
#   FP8 row) turns it off and keeps the bytes. Where the driver lacks virtual memory support it
#   falls back to the estimate; whether gfx1151's does is unread.
# - The default --block-size is 64, was 16 (#63231). No row names one, so each moves to 64, but
#   ROCm's paged attention keeps 16.
# - It fixes caches undersized by up to 84% on DGX Spark (#65413), the GB10s' platform.
# The task's benchmarks ran on v0.33.0 and were not rerun on v0.34.0.
VLLM_RELEASE=v0.34.0
VLLM_REPOSITORY_CUDA=vllm/vllm-openai
VLLM_REPOSITORY_ROCM=vllm/vllm-openai-rocm
VLLM_ROWS=vllm-rows
VLLM_MODEL_CUDA=gemma-4-26B-A4B-NVFP4
VLLM_MODEL_ROCM=gpt-oss-120b

# Native vLLM's Python (vllm-native.sh): the CPython minor version uv installs for each release's
# virtualenv. Held on 3.12, the image's Python, so the two hosting methods differ only in how they
# are hosted, and currency reports Python behind its latest until it moves. Native vLLM is retired
# on both hosts, so nothing moves it now: it stays held until vLLM's pins are removed.
VLLM_NATIVE_PYTHON=3.12
